# File: specs/336-fix-final-head-evidence-hang-on-workflow-qualified-check-names/feature.gherkin
#
# Generated from: specs/336-fix-final-head-evidence-hang-on-workflow-qualified-check-names/requirements.md
Feature: Fix final-head evidence hang on workflow-qualified check names
  Final-head collection previously polled forever when verification
  recorded workflow-qualified check names and GitHub returned bare job
  names. Matching now uses one canonical workflow-plus-job identity.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Qualified declarations complete H1-to-H2 collection
    Given verification declared "Python CI / verify" and "nmg-sdlc contribution gate / Validate nmg-sdlc contribution evidence"
    And H2 GitHub checks report job names "verify" and "Validate nmg-sdlc contribution evidence" with those workflows, SUCCESS, pull_request, and URLs
    When final-head evidence collection runs
    Then collection completes with one satisfied evidence item per declaration
    And it does not keep polling after those successful checks are visible

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Same job name from different workflows fails closed
    Given two successful pull_request checks named "verify" from different workflows
    When collection matches a declaration that does not uniquely select one workflow
    Then collection fails closed immediately
    And it does not treat either check as the other by suffix or trailing-name matching

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Unique bare names still match
    Given a declaration named "contract-tests"
    And GitHub reports one pull_request check named "contract-tests" with empty workflow metadata, SUCCESS, and a URL on the exact head
    When evidence collection runs
    Then that declaration is satisfied
    And unique bare-name delivery still reaches final-head validation

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Pending stays pending and terminal mismatch does not hang
    Given a declared check identity that has not appeared or is still pending
    When collection observes that state
    Then it keeps waiting
    Given pull_request checks for that head are already successful, skipped, or failed and the declared identity cannot be uniquely resolved
    When collection observes that state
    Then it fails closed immediately rather than polling forever
    And missing URL, wrong event, or wrong head is a failure, not a wait

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Canonical identity is shared and fail-closed
    Given verifier production, readiness parsing, snapshot collection, final-head matching, delivery-validation markers, and hosted evidence
    When they record or match a required check or check run
    Then they use the same canonical identity
    And that identity is workflow plus job when workflow metadata is present, or the unique bare job name when workflow is empty
    And collisions, wrong workflow, wrong event, wrong head, missing URL, and matched pending or failing checks are rejected

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Exact-name fixtures still deliver
    Given controlled-draft delivery where declaration names already equal GitHub check names
    When H1-to-H2 collection and merge proof run
    Then delivery still succeeds without requiring workflow metadata
